d 'COMBINEALL': module to combine (append, merge, or joinby) or convert every file in a directory
d
d  combineall sweeps a directory and combines every file of one
d type (.dta, CSV and other delimited text, Excel, or XML) into a
d single dataset by append, merge, or joinby, or converts the files
d to .dta and stops (convertonly). The engine dates to 2011
d (v1.0.0). v2.0.0 adds a harmonization layer under cmethod(append)
d for stacking yearly file releases whose element names mutate
d across vintages: map(renames.csv) applies only the renames whose
d [firstyear,lastyear] window covers the 4-digit year extracted
d from each filename, generates int year, records provenance in
d char varname[source], and prints a variable-by-year harmonization
d table. strict turns absent-oldname reports into errors. Replaces
d the panelstack package. combineall using "built/panel",
d cmethod(append) map(renames.csv) 
d
d KW: append; merge; joinby; import; convert; panel; harmonize; rename; vintage
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
d Author: Elizabeth Teas, Far Harbor, LLC
d Support: email elizabeth@@farharbor.com
d
f combineall.ado
f combineall.sthlp
